@inject TimeProvider Clock

@*
    What a page that follows what changes writes under its heading (NFR-USA-1): that it updates
    by itself, with a link that pauses it, and on a page that is paused since when it is as it
    is, with a link that has it follow again. A page that changes by itself can be stopped by
    whoever reads it slowly, reads it with a screen reader, or is put off by what moves.

    The link leads to the same page, with the choice in its address and every other choice of
    the address as it is. The choice is of this page as it is open now: nothing is stored for
    it, another screen follows again, and so does this one when it is opened anew. What the
    page says of itself is read out by a screen reader when it changes, which is when the link
    was followed.

    An address that makes a choice that there is not has no page, as an address with a page
    number that is none has not: the page itself answers that, as it answers a page number, and
    nothing is written here then. LiveUpdates writes the parts of the page for both cases. The
    texts are in LivePages. See "Pausing" in docs/live-updates.md.
*@

@if (_paused is { } paused && HttpContext is { } request)
{
    <p class="live-pause">
        <span role="status">@(paused ? LivePages.PausedAt(Clock.GetUtcNow(), Times) : LivePages.Follows)@(paused && Prices ? $" {LivePages.PausedPrices}" : string.Empty)</span>
        <a href="@LivePages.AddressOf(request.Request, !paused)">@(paused ? LivePages.Resume : LivePages.Pause)</a>
    </p>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The times of the page: every time is written in its time zone (NFR-USA-3). See docs/times.md.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter]
    private PageTimes Times { get; set; } = PageTimes.Utc;

    private bool? _paused;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the page shows prices that are read while a page follows them: a paused page
    /// says then that it may have none.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Prices { get; set; }

    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (HttpContext is { } request)
        {
            _paused = LivePages.PausedOf(request.Request.Query);
        }
    }
}
